      {
        "id": "lem-vc-loss-rademacher-bound",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "VC entropy bound for empirical Rademacher complexity",
        "deps": [
          "def-shattered-set-and-vc-dimension",
          "def-vc-subgraph-class-and-index",
          "def-product-sigma-algebra-and-finite-product-sigma-algebras",
          "thm-vc-covering-entropy",
          "lem-bounded-variable-hoeffding-mgf",
          "thm-geometric-series",
          "def-natural-logarithm",
          "thm-natural-logarithm-laws",
          "thm-exponential-two-point-convexity"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 1,
        "justified_by": [],
        "statement": "Let $(\\mathcal X,\\Sigma)$ be a nonempty measurable space and let $H$ be a nonempty class of measurable binary functions on $\\mathcal X$ with finite VC dimension $d$. Put $\\mathcal Z=\\mathcal X\\times\\{0,1\\}$ with its product sigma-algebra and $G_H=\\{g_h:h\\in H\\}$, where $g_h(x,y)=\\mathbf1\\{h(x)\\ne y\\}$. For any integer $m\\ge1$ and any fixed sample $S=(z_1,\\ldots,z_m)\\in\\mathcal Z^m$, let $\\sigma_1,\\ldots,\\sigma_m$ be independent uniform signs and define\n\n$$\\widehat{\\mathfrak R}_S(G_H):=\\mathbb E_\\sigma\\sup_{h\\in H}\\frac1m\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sigma_i g_h(z_i).$$\n\nSet $K_0:=3e^2/(e-1)$, $K:=4K_0$, $A:=12eK+2$, and\n\n$$C_{\\rm VC}:=3\\sqrt{8A}\\left(\\sqrt{\\log A}+2\\sqrt{\\log 2}\\right).$$\n\nThen, for every such finite sample,\n\n$$\\widehat{\\mathfrak R}_S(G_H)\\le C_{\\rm VC}\\sqrt{\\frac{d+1}{m}}.$$\n\nNo countability or Axiom of Choice premise is used; the supremum over classifiers reduces to the finite set of loss traces on $S$."
      },
